{
  "date": "2026-10-25",
  "scope": "Actual catalog critical-section dispatcher under separate lock/open/context/refresh/callback contracts. Two native callback-scope defects were reproduced and fixed. Complete native adapter/history refinement remains open.",
  "properties": {
    "catalog_transaction::execute": "Bound nonnested entry, original-lock identity, at-most-once callback, final success context, returning-path active-guard cleanup and unchanged early rejected state.",
    "catalog_transaction::locked": "Fresh identity checked before install; successful locked refresh before activation and callback; final binding/active/ready check; identity errors have an actual mismatch and no changed catalog view.",
    "catalog_transaction::effect": "Exact Result-to-Failure mapping without erasing the error variant.",
    "catalog_transaction::finish": "Preserves an operation error even when unlock fails; unlock failure prevents a successful operation from returning success."
  },
  "runtime_changes": "Catalog::transaction calls the verified generic dispatcher through stack adapters. LockedCatalog borrows the original Catalog privately and exposes read-only Deref plus explicit operation forwarding, preventing mutable ownership/borrow escape. A stack invocation flag invalidates LogState if the callback unwinds. The existing filesystem operations, synchronization order, file format and error messages are retained; no additional heap allocation or payload copy. Runtime flags/forwarding exist; no zero-overhead measurement claim.",
  "api_compatibility": "Rust Catalog::transaction and Config::catalog callbacks now take &mut LockedCatalog instead of &mut Catalog. Inferred closures with normal operations retain their syntax; explicit argument annotations and helper functions taking &mut Catalog need migration. Python APIs and persisted formats are unchanged. Release/version audit remains pending.",
  "bugs": [
    {
      "name": "caught_catalog_callback_unwind_allows_direct_write",
      "before": "After a callback panic was caught, new transaction entry rejected the active marker but direct pack could still see ready state and append after the lock had unwound.",
      "fix": "Native Transaction keeps an invocation guard; Drop invalidates the catalog LogState when callback execution unwinds. The interrupted active marker remains, so subsequent entry requires reopening.",
      "baseline": "The strengthened native regression failed because pack returned Ok after the caught panic; 1 test executed and failed.",
      "baseline_source_sha256": {
        "rust/gc.rs": "3e772d8120b2f4505aa772071a71d2ba1957d220f9bf0dd00b4688b9ea3e6ab1",
        "rust/catalog_transaction.rs": "6fb8879a51f220220224d4155578139907c1347e75ab1b0c9e621bc85100eeb7"
      },
      "baseline_log_sha256": "7a5815d2bd454776990e0cc9892fb18545bfa7ee868484558e1ea76c9e2feed3",
      "regression": "gc::replay_tests::caught_callback_unwind_requires_reopen_and_preserves_committed_effects"
    },
    {
      "name": "active_catalog_ownership_escapes_callback",
      "before": "Safe Rust mem::replace moved the active Catalog out of its callback. An error ended the outer transaction but the moved object retained active/ready state and wrote successfully while a different descriptor held the catalog lock.",
      "fix": "The public callback receives LockedCatalog with a private borrowed Catalog and no DerefMut. Type/lifetime checks reject taking the Catalog, obtaining a mutable Catalog through dereferencing, or storing the callback borrow outside its scope.",
      "baseline": "The executable external-crate witness ran 1 test and failed because the escaped pack write succeeded under another descriptor lock.",
      "baseline_source_sha256": {
        "rust/gc.rs": "b7a340842c0f782bf1e65fb5948ebb71bbcddfaf75d2dbeb2abed2621439b913",
        "witness.rs": "77857375de4fa51445f12b20a6c2c9e66d83a5896c29662ecdf65661552be225"
      },
      "baseline_log_sha256": "1864bbba84cb077eac3470349f2264194c431bbb6ba5758221e34616289b0669",
      "witness_source": "use straw::{Error, Result, gc::Catalog, store::Config};\n#[test]\nfn moving_catalog_out_of_callback_must_not_preserve_write_authority() -> Result<()> {\n    let directory = tempfile::tempdir()?;\n    let config = Config::new(directory.path().to_str().unwrap(), \"escape\", vec![\"bytes.v1\".into()], 1024, 1024, 1024)?;\n    let mut catalog = Catalog::open(&config)?;\n    let mut escaped = None;\n    let result = catalog.transaction(&config, |active| -> Result<()> {\n        escaped = Some(std::mem::replace(active, Catalog::open(&config)?));\n        Err(Error::new(\"CallbackFailed\", \"moved active catalog\"))\n    });\n    assert!(result.is_err());\n    let mut escaped = escaped.unwrap();\n    let contender = std::fs::File::open(config.root.join(\"storage.log\"))?;\n    contender.try_lock().unwrap();\n    let result = escaped.pack(&config, \"raw/escaped\", true, &mut |_| Ok(()));\n    assert!(result.is_err(), \"moved catalog wrote while another descriptor held the lock\");\n    Ok(())\n}\n",
      "regression": "LockedCatalog positive example and E0308/E0596/E0521 compiler-negative examples in rust/gc.rs"
    }
  ],
  "boundaries": [
    "These two bugs were found by reviewing the unproved native callback mapping and running witnesses; the conditional dispatcher proof did not automatically discover them.",
    "ENV-CATALOG-TRANSACTION separately retains native lock/open/metadata, actual initial context, refresh/callback/guard mapping, complete durable history and contention progress. Legal callbacks must preserve identity/recovery provenance when leaving an active context.",
    "Successful acquisition establishes the lock; failed acquire/release may retain effects. No unconditional all-error lock-release theorem is asserted.",
    "Verus proves returning Result paths, not arbitrary Rust unwinding, Rust borrow-checker soundness, compiler behavior or filesystem implementation. Native regressions and compiler examples are separate evidence.",
    "No new library primitive, admitted straw body or external_body was added. Complete distributed/WAL/GC and writer-retirement obligations remain open."
  ],
